{
  "version": 1,
  "notes": [
    "Region-level redaction fixtures. Each scene is painted synthetically in-test (no photo GT needed): sensitive boxes in one color, keep boxes in another.",
    "Regions carry a canonical type + confidence 0.9 and flow through the real planner + renderer + verifier.",
    "Correct redaction: an applied op covers >=95% of a GT box area (coverage).",
    "Recall: GT boxes with coverage >= 0.95 divided by all GT boxes.",
    "Precision: applied ops covering >= 95% of at least one GT box, divided by all applied ops. Overlap merging is legitimate (security wins), so IoU is the wrong precision rule here: a merged union correctly covers several boxes at once.",
    "Over-redaction bound: applied op area <= 3x the union area of the GT boxes it covers. Padding is intentional; the bound catches runaway boxes while tolerating legitimate merges.",
    "All values are synthetic."
  ],
